# Frontend Rules — SolidJS

**This is SolidJS, not React.** No `useState`, `useEffect`, or React hooks.

## Tooling

- Vite 6 + SolidJS 1.9
- **Biome** for lint/format — `make web-format`, `make web-lint` (not ESLint/Prettier)

## Structure

```
web/frontend/src/
  App.tsx           main page
  api.ts            all fetch/API calls
  components/       UI pieces
  lib/persist.ts    localStorage keys (encode settings)
  lib/format.ts     bytes/speed/progress helpers
  styles/app.css    global styles
```

## Encode UI

- `EditToolsCard.tsx` — encode tool tab; advanced section is opt-in
- Settings persist: `jav-downloader-encode-settings`, `jav-downloader-remember-encode`
- Tooltips via `FieldHint` for technical controls

## Dev vs production

- Dev: `make web-api` (:8765) + `make web-dev` (:5173, proxies `/api`)
- Production: `make web-build` → output to `src/jav_downloader/web/static/`

## After any UI change

```bash
make web-build
git add src/jav_downloader/web/static/
```

Termux users have no Node — committed static bundle is required.

## Constraints

- Keep UI lightweight for mobile/Termux
- Do not add heavy frontend dependencies without good reason
- Never edit files under `src/jav_downloader/web/static/` directly
